## 1. Syntax Overview & Type System

The `.sovra` language is a static, zero-overhead domain-specific language designed for high-concurrency multi-agent orchestration, lock-free shared memory state graphs, and compile-time taint tracking.

### 1.1 Primitive & Security-Bounded Types

| Type Identifier | Description | Compiler Memory Tag | AST Lattice Rules |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `candidate<T>` | Raw, untrusted input payload from network, STT, or external tools. | `0xDEAD` (TAINTED) | Cannot be passed to execution sinks. Cannot implicitly coerce to `decision<T>`. |
| `decision<T>` | Certified, policy-validated data structure. | `0xBEAF` (CERTIFIED) | Eligible for system sinks (`system.execute`, file I/O, IPC). Must originate from a `gate(...)` sanitizer block. |
| `SHM_RingBuffer` | Multi-agent lock-free ring buffer slot pointer. | `0x1000` (Base) | Constrained stack allocation `[sp, #0]`. |
| `HyperVector` | 10,000-bit topological bitset arena reference. | `0x2000` (Arena) | Constrained stack allocation `[sp, #8]`. |

